_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 9
---
order: 9
---
short_label: XII.9
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: In equal pyramids with triangular bases the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights; and those pyramids are equal in which the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights.
----
proof:

Let there be equal pyramids with triangular bases {ABC} and {DEF} and vertices {G} and {H}.

I say that in the pyramids {ABCG|pABCG} and {DEFH|pDEFH} the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights, that is the base {ABC} is to the base {DEF} as the height of the pyramid {DEFH|pDEFH} is to the height of the pyramid {ABCG|pABCG}.

Complete the parallelepipedal solids *BGML* and *EHQP.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="400" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XII.9 diagram" src="propXII9.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The pyramids are given; the one construction is completing the two
    // parallelepipeds, after which the walk is highlight beats. The converse
    // sets out the pyramids alone, then restores the solids at "With the
    // same construction".
    //
    // A polyhedron draws no highlight, so the two pyramids get faceless
    // wireframe twins, octagons that walk all six edges (pABCG, pDEFH;
    // prose refs use the display override). The solids BGML and EHQP are
    // lit through their six faces (BOX1, BOX2; A2 is the eighth corner of
    // BGML, unlabelled in Joyce's figure). Joyce's ABCM already spans the
    // base BM but is a helper for the application; BM is its own target.
    // The heights are not drawn: the figure is built flat in the floor
    // plane, so a foot from G or H has no length. Every added element is
    // transparent, so the resting figure is unchanged.
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): B, E, D (lineSliders) and F
    // (planeSlider) are givens; M (planeSlider) and a (lineSlider) are
    // corners of BGML, arriving only when the solid is completed, so they
    // are deferred. Every other point is derived.
    var PYR   = ["A","B","C","G","D","E","F","H","ABCG","DEFH",
                 "ABC","DEF","pABCG","pDEFH"];
    var BOX1  = ["BM","BMtop","BMfr","BMbk","BMlf","BMrt"];
    var BOX2  = ["EQ","EQtop","EQfr","EQbk","EQlf","EQrt"];
    var ALL   = PYR.concat(["Apar","Dpar","M","a","L","Q","O","P","R"],
                           BOX1, BOX2);
    var BOXES = BOX1.concat(BOX2);
    var PYRS  = ["pABCG","pDEFH"];
